config-connector-extensions patch 0013: mockgcp keeps a deleted Cloud SQL backup run, with status DELETED, as the real API does.

Written here, on top of patch 0003 (upstream PR #12553's mockgcp), for
sqladmin.gcp.hfl.dev SQLAdminBackup. A live run against a real project
(docs/live-runs.md, 2026-11-09) showed that after backupRuns.delete
completes, backupRuns.get still returns the run with status DELETED rather
than 404; patch 0003's mock removed it. Now backupRuns.delete marks the run
DELETED and keeps it. Deleting a run already DELETED answers 404 (not seen
live; the simplest choice).

Upstream candidate: yes, with PR #12553, whose mock and
controller assume a deleted run is gone.

diff --git a/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackup.go b/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackup.go
--- a/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackup.go
+++ b/mockgcp/mocksql/sqlbackup.go
@@ -127,13 +127,23 @@
 
 	fqn := name.String()
 
+	// Cloud SQL keeps a deleted backup run: backupRuns.get still returns it,
+	// with status DELETED (seen against the real API, docs/live-runs.md in
+	// config-connector-extensions). Deleting it again is taken as not found.
 	deleted := &pb.BackupRun{}
-	if err := s.storage.Delete(ctx, fqn, deleted); err != nil {
+	if err := s.storage.Get(ctx, fqn, deleted); err != nil {
 		if status.Code(err) == codes.NotFound {
 			return nil, status.Errorf(codes.NotFound, "Not Found")
 		}
 		return nil, err
 	}
+	if deleted.Status == pb.SqlBackupRunStatus_DELETED {
+		return nil, status.Errorf(codes.NotFound, "Not Found")
+	}
+	deleted.Status = pb.SqlBackupRunStatus_DELETED
+	if err := s.storage.Update(ctx, fqn, deleted); err != nil {
+		return nil, err
+	}
 
 	op := &pb.Operation{
 		TargetProject: name.Project.ID,
